      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T18:32:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This configuration results with:\n4096 × (10 × 32768 × 4 − 10) \u003d 5,368,668,160 sectors\nvssim_config_manager.h defines ssd_config-\u003esectors_in_ssd as uint32_t.\nThis overflows.\nAs far as I understand the filesystem tests do not catch it since they use different configurations. Also, vssim.c does not check FTL_WRITE_SECT function\u0027s return values, hence the tests do not actually verify its return value as well.\nI understand it\u0027s a template, and it is probably for @davidsa@openu.ac.il to decide whether its time to update in a separate ticket and I write it here as a heads up.\nChanging this will probably cause modifications in other areas for it to work properly (without adding warnings or even errors), making it out of scope for this change.",
